analysis domain : 112 x 78 at full-plane origin (9, 6) -- Crop is applied BEFORE luma, variance, weighting and accumulation
--- the merge ---
bands           : 3 Laplacian levels + 1 base, coarsest 14 x 10
selection       : SOFT -- weight = (band power above the noise floor)^exponent, a convex combination.
                  Sign coherence is free: a convex combination cannot take adjacent
                  coefficients from opposite-signed frames, which is the ringing a
                  coefficient-wise argmax produces.
noise gate      : 2.00 x the modelled band-noise power. Below it, NO frame may win and the
                  merge averages -- which is the correct estimator when there is no
                  information, and the only operation that gets below single-frame noise.
exponent        : 2.00
per-band exp    : 2 3 4   (coarsest -> finest)
                  sharpness ramps 1.4x per octave toward the fine bands. A wrong pick in a
                  fine band is one high-frequency coefficient nobody can see; a wrong pick
                  in a coarse band IS the rim.
base band       : plain mean across frames
not applied     : photometric gain, clip census, outlier rejection, halo correction, through-focus
                  statistics. Those are the --merge estimator path's stages; this arm is the merge only.
alignment       : ON (M194d-independent), reference frame 2, 5 placed / 0 refused, 0.0 s
  held-out err  : NOT MEASURED   resampler: CatmullRom
  coverage      : CROPPED to the region EVERY frame covers -- 112 x 78 plane px at (9, 6) of 137 x 95, emitted at UNITY SCALE. 0.0% of width dropped and NOT upsampled (k=1.0000), so the output is SMALLER than the plane by design and no placement carries a coverage scale. The reference frame's own placement reaches the gather unmodified.
memory plan     : 5 canonical chunks, 1 reusable frame worker, 1 retained + 1 scratch accumulator, 2 execution threads
                  CONSTANT in the frame count and reduction order. Chunks run serially; spatial work uses
                  the execution pool. STREHL_PYRAMID_WORKERS=N changes threads, never arithmetic.

folded          : 5 / 5 frames in 0.1 s (0.03 s per frame, 2 execution threads)
band noise gain : 0.8894 0.0529 0.0101 0.0037
                  (E[L_k^2] / sigma_0^2, MEASURED on these operators, not derived.)
measured floor  : 0.7779 0.0487
                  x white       : 0.8746 0.9200
                  THE FLOOR THE GATE ACTUALLY USED, averaged over 5 warped
  frames. The line above it is the white-noise constant, which is
  exact only for an UNWARPED frame; resampling correlates neighbours
                  and moves the per-band split. Bands past this list kept the constant.
                  STREHL_GATE_FLOOR=white restores it everywhere.
weight fallback : 0.0% 0.0% 0.0% 100.0%
                  FloorPedestalV1 experimental: zero-total-weight fallback fraction.
Positive equal weights also average; this is not an averaging fraction.

